From Engineering on #383 (Stage 7 part A).

1. **Container tool.** This Mac has no Docker, Podman or Colima, so neither the image build nor the Tester's click-through against the container can run. Options:
   - (a) Colima via Homebrew: free, open source, command line;
   - (b) Docker Desktop: free for personal and small-business use under its licence terms;
   - (c) skip the local container test and test on Render directly.
   PM recommends (a).
2. **Address data on a fresh hosted disk.** Everything else is fetched on demand from public sources (TIGER, CCRS, Caltrans postmiles and counts, Overpass). NAD address points (426 MB CA extract) and TIGER ADDRFEAT (180 MB) have no fetcher. Without them, house-address crashes go to review instead of being placed (D5, #315). Options:
   - (a) ship without them for now; those crashes go to review;
   - (b) an on-demand per-county ADDRFEAT fetcher, plus a one-time upload of the NAD CA file to the Render disk;
   - (c) bake both into the image (~600 MB more on every deploy).
   Engineering and PM recommend (b).

Waiting on the user's answer in the PM chat.
